{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/219105-attribute-caps-godhood-and-the-character-sheet","id":219105,"title":"Attribute caps, Godhood, and the character sheet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-05T08:28:48-07:00","id":219105,"title":"Attribute caps, Godhood, and the character sheet","content":"This has been bothering me, and I thought to finally just ask.<br /> <br /> The god character sheet has ten dots for mundane attributes, ten dots for epic attributes, and the &quot;ultimate star&quot;. It's abundantly clear mundane attributes go to 11, and here and there are referrals to mundane attributes of 12 (the &quot;epic strength in perspective&quot; sidebar on pg. 61 of <i>God</i> among others) yet none of the Legend 12 gods with stats have them (least and most glaring of all, when those gods have respective ultimate attributes), But...the character sheet is what it is.<br /> <br /> So, how on Earth does this work? Do mundane attributes go to 12, and if so what is the incentive (because I'm not seeing any, save one extra die that at that level is pretty trivial for a 44 experience cost), or is that an editing error? The intent players have to buy the mundane attribute to 11, <i>then</i> get their ultimate, is fairly clear but how is that recorded on the character sheet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T14:51:35-07:00","id":219498,"title":"","content":"This is one of the many questions that Scion's original development team just did not think too hard about. Yes, assume that Mundane Attributes scale up to 11.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T18:41:53-07:00","id":219718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/219105-attribute-caps-godhood-and-the-character-sheet#post219105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how on Earth does this work? Do mundane attributes go to 12, and if so what is the incentive (because I'm not seeing any, save one extra die that at that level is pretty trivial for a 44 experience cost), or is that an editing error? The intent players have to buy the mundane attribute to 11, <i>then</i> get their ultimate, is fairly clear but how is that recorded on the character sheet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mundane Attributes can technically go up to 12, because the cap on Attributes = Permanent Legend. However, you are absolutely correct that there is no incentive beyond a single die and higher lifting capacity, etc. It is an opportunity cost that no player I have ever met would take. So you might as well imagine it does not exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 08-08-2014, 06:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T13:06:48-07:00","id":221234,"title":"","content":"Yea Attributes go up to 12. Just a 12th dot is a nasty XP sink for little reward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-de